asurement system: an intra-tester reliability study</article-title><source>Man Ther</source><year>2003</year><volume>8</volume><issue>3</issue><fpage>176</fpage><lpage>179</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1356-689X(03)00009-2</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12909439</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><label>6.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Antonaci</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Bulgheroni</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghirmai</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lanfranchi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dalla Toffola</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Sandrini</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Nappi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>3D kinematic analysis and clinical evaluation of neck movements in patients with whiplash injury</article-title><source>Cephalalgia</source><year>2002</year><volume>22</volume><issue>7</issue><fpage>533</fpage><lpage>542</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1468-2982.2002.00405.x</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12230595</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><label>7.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Assink</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergman</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Knoester</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Winters</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Dijkstra</surname><given-names>PU</given-names></name><name><surname>Postema</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interobserver reliability of neck-mobility measurement by means of the flock-of-birds electromagnetic tracking system</article-title><source>J Manipulative Physiol Ther</source><year>2005</year><volume>28</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>408</fpage><lpage>413</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jmpt.2005.06.009</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16096040</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><label>8.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balogun</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Abereoje</surname><given-names>OK</given-names></name><name><surname>Olaogun</surname><given-names>MO</given-names></name><name><surname>Obajuluwa</surname><given-names>VA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Inter and intratester reliability of measuring neck motions with tape measure and Myrin gravity-reference goniometer</article-title><source>J Orthop Sports Phys Ther</source><year>1989</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>248</fpage><lpage>253</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bergman</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Knoester</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Assink</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Dijkstra</surname><given-names>PU</given-names></name><name><surname>Winters</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Variation in the cervical range of motion over time measured by the &#x0201c;flock of birds&#x0201d; electromagnetic tracking system</article-title><source>Spine</source><year>2005</year><volume>30</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>650</fpage><lpage>654</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.brs.0000155414.03723.3d</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15770180</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bogduk</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person